{#
    The chosen path, as a centred modal at every width - same backdrop,
    glass-card and m-5 as the withdraw/decline dialogs, so they read as one
    family. The panel used to sit inline under four cards, where a phone user
    never saw it.

    No JavaScript: the purpose radios drive it, and Back and close are labels
    that select pp-none. Must live inside the .group wrapper in
    _purpose_chooser.html.twig.

    Context: document, form, hasUsableCertificate.
#}
<div class="hidden group-has-[#pp-self:checked]:flex group-has-[#pp-then:checked]:flex group-has-[#pp-only:checked]:flex group-has-[#pp-deliver:checked]:flex
            fixed inset-0 z-[1050] h-full w-full items-center justify-center overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden
            bg-theme-headings/40 backdrop-blur-sm modal-backdrop-fade">

    {# Click-outside-to-close. #}
    <label for="pp-none" class="absolute inset-0"><span class="sr-only">Close</span></label>

    <div class="relative m-5 max-h-[90vh] w-full max-w-md overflow-y-auto glass-card !bg-white sm:!bg-white/90 modal-card">

        {# In flow rather than absolute, so no panel heading can run under it.
           Back and close both select pp-none: from here "back" is back to
           choosing a purpose, which is the page behind this modal. #}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-3 pt-3">
            <label for="pp-none" class="inline-flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-1 rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-theme-secondarytextcolor hover:bg-theme-activebg hover:text-theme-headings">
                <i class="ti ti-chevron-left text-base leading-none" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                Back
            </label>
            <label for="pp-none" class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-theme-secondarytextcolor hover:bg-theme-activebg hover:text-theme-headings">
                <i class="ti ti-x text-base leading-none" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="sr-only">Close</span>
            </label>
        </div>

        <div class="px-6 pb-6">

            {# ── I sign it myself: certificate and PIN, no second step ──────── #}
            <div class="hidden group-has-[#pp-self:checked]:block">
                <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-theme-secondarytextcolor">Step 2 of 2</p>
                <h3 class="mt-0.5 mb-4 text-base font-bold text-theme-headings">Sign it with your certificate</h3>
                {{ include('signing/_sign_panel.html.twig') }}
            </div>

            {# ── The three paths that need other people ─────────────────────── #}
            <div class="hidden group-has-[#pp-then:checked]:block">
                <h3 class="mb-3 text-base font-bold text-theme-headings">You are in the queue</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-bodycolor">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-users mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>You name the signers next and set the order by dragging. You start last, but you can sign at any position.</span></li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-clock mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Strict order: signer 2 cannot sign before signer 1. Deadline 7 days by default, 30 at most.</span></li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-circle-check mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>A signer may decline, with an optional reason. That closes the request.</span></li>
                </ul>
                <a href="{{ path('app_signing_request_new', {id: document.id, include_me: 1}) }}"
                   class="btn btn-primary mt-4 w-full inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
                    Choose the signers <i class="ti ti-chevron-right text-base leading-none" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </a>
                <p class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-theme-secondarytextcolor">Nothing is sent until you confirm.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="hidden group-has-[#pp-only:checked]:block">
                <h3 class="mb-3 text-base font-bold text-theme-headings">The queue will not include you</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-bodycolor">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-users mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>You name the signers and their order next. You are not in the queue and will not be asked to sign.</span></li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-clock mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Strict order: signer 2 cannot sign before signer 1. Deadline 7 days by default, 30 at most.</span></li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-circle-check mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>A signer may decline, with an optional reason. That closes the request.</span></li>
                </ul>
                <a href="{{ path('app_signing_request_new', {id: document.id}) }}"
                   class="btn btn-primary mt-4 w-full inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
                    Choose the signers <i class="ti ti-chevron-right text-base leading-none" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </a>
                <p class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-theme-secondarytextcolor">Nothing is sent until you confirm.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="hidden group-has-[#pp-deliver:checked]:block">
                <h3 class="mb-3 text-base font-bold text-theme-headings">Delivery asks nothing in return</h3>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-bodycolor">
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-mail-forward mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>You name the recipients next. Everyone is served at the same moment, in no particular order.</span></li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-lock mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>A delivery cannot be refused and nothing is asked of a recipient. There is no deadline.</span></li>
                    <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><i class="ti ti-circle-check mt-0.5 text-base leading-none text-theme-secondarytextcolor" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Delivery is final: once served, the document is finished.</span></li>
                </ul>
                <a href="{{ path('app_delivery_new', {id: document.id}) }}"
                   class="btn btn-primary mt-4 w-full inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
                    Choose the recipients <i class="ti ti-chevron-right text-base leading-none" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </a>
                <p class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-theme-secondarytextcolor">Nothing is served until you confirm.</p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
